00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:56.600
the speak method, and it's five changes

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:59.840
that take your words from self-sabotage

00:09:56.600 --> 00:10:02.040
to self-creation. S, state what you

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:04.080
want, never what you fear. Most people's

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:06.560
inner monologue is organized around

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.720
avoidance. I don't want to be broke. I

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.680
don't want to be alone. I hope I don't

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:12.760
mess this up. But the truth is, your

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:14.200
subconscious mind does not process

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:16.200
negation very well. So, when you're

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:18.640
saying things like, "I don't want to be

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:21.400
broke," your brain lights up the concept

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:24.000
of broke and starts orienting around it.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:25.920
So, it becomes like an obsession around

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.840
the word broke. And the more focused you

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.560
are on something, the more you're

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.920
creating more of it. Neurolinguistic

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.440
research shows that suppression

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:33.280
commands, like, "I don't think of a

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:35.240
white bear," actually increases the

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.280
frequency of that repressed thought.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:39.240
Your brain has to hold the concept

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:41.440
active in order to monitor whether

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.600
you're successfully avoiding it or not.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:45.120
So, instead of saying things like, "I

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:46.880
don't want to be broke," you can say,

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:49.000
"I'm building wealth." Instead of

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:51.320
saying, "I don't want to be alone," say,

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.760
"I'm attracting deeper and healthier

00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:54.680
love." And instead of saying, "I hope I

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:56.680
don't mess this up," you say, "I'm

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:58.720
prepared for this." Do you feel the

00:10:56.680 --> 00:11:01.400
difference? It's the same thing and the

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.000
same desire, same wants, but completely

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:05.960
different ways of speaking it into

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:08.400
existence. P, present tense only. Your

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:09.680
brain responds to language literally. If

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.960
you're saying things like, "I will be

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:12.520
confident," you're telling your brain

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:15.280
that confidence is somewhere in the

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:17.520
future. It's always coming. It's never

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:19.640
here right now. Just like how the diet

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:21.680
always starts tomorrow, but now we're no

00:11:19.640 --> 00:11:23.440
longer doing that. It already started.

00:11:21.680 --> 00:11:25.360
We're already doing it. We're done,

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:27.720
basically. We're already done. "I am

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:30.000
confident" tells your brain this is

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:31.600
happening right now. Your reticular

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.080
activating system, which is the filter

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:34.960
in your brain that decides what you pay

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:37.240
attention to, starts scanning for even

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:39.680
more evidence to confirm whatever you're

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:41.600
declaring in the present tense. So, say

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:42.960
I am creative, and your brain starts

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:44.840
noticing all the ways that you're

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:46.960
already being creative. And when you're

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:49.360
saying things like, "I will be creative

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:50.720
someday," your brain files it away as,

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:52.200
"You know what? This is not important

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:54.200
right now. I'll deal with that later."

00:11:52.200 --> 00:11:56.520
So, someday you're going to be creative,

00:11:54.200 --> 00:11:59.480
but not today. The present tense is the

00:11:56.520 --> 00:12:01.120
spell, but the future tense is the wish

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:02.560
unfulfilled. If you want something to

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:05.080
come true right now, you better speak it

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:07.080
in present tense. E, embody it when you

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:09.120
say it. Most people, they will say

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:10.560
words, but their body doesn't believe

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.080
them. You're saying things like, "I am

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:14.160
confident," while your whole body is

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:16.000
hunched over, and your energy is just

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.920
not feeling it. So, your body is sending

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.600
a completely different signal through

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.480
your words. And guess what wins that

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.680
argument every time? It's your body. Amy

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:25.880
Cuddy's original research at Harvard

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:28.080
found that power posing, standing tall

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:29.760
and taking up space with your chest open

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.720
for just 2 minutes, made people feel

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.960
significantly

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:34.880
more powerful and confident. Now, I want

00:12:32.960 --> 00:12:36.680
to be transparent once again, because

00:12:34.880 --> 00:12:38.280
the actual hormonal specific claims in

00:12:36.680 --> 00:12:40.520
the original 2010 study has been

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:42.720
challenged in replications. But, what

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:44.760
still held up consistently across

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:46.960
meta-analyses is the psychological

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:48.720
effect. Your posture changes how

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:51.120
powerful you're feeling, which changes

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:53.160
what feels possible to you. Your body

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.360
sends signals to your brain about what

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:57.320
state you're in. So, when you speak your

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:59.440
declarations out loud, you better stand

00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:01.480
up and put your shoulders back, speak

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:02.720
from your chest, and your diaphragm, and

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.960
not from your throat. If you can't

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.120
remember all of these things, then

00:13:03.960 --> 00:13:07.960
basically use your stomach to talk.

00:13:06.120 --> 00:13:09.560
That's what I do. I will speak like

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:12.480
this, and I sound like a tiny mouse when

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:14.360
I do it. So, use your body in your

00:13:12.480 --> 00:13:15.800
speech, and let your body match the

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:17.640
vibrations of the words. Some of you

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:18.760
guys actually clown on me saying that

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:20.720
like, "Oh my gosh, you speak like an

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:23.560
Italian." But guess what? I speak with

00:13:20.720 --> 00:13:25.200
my entire physical body, and my mind,

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:27.000
and my spirit. I speak with everything I

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:29.560
got. So, maybe that's why you guys

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:32.400
listen to me. A, attach emotion. A

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:34.480
declaration without emotion is just a

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:35.880
sentence. Your amygdala, which is the

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:37.640
emotional processing center of your

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.800
brain, it tags experiences and

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:41.840
information with emotional weight. The

00:13:39.800 --> 00:13:44.520
stronger the emotion that's attached to

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:46.040
a memory or a statement, the deeper it

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:47.760
feels and then the more powerful it

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:49.960
gets. This is why you remember where you

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:51.480
were during a life-changing moment, but

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:53.720
you can't even remember what you ate for

00:13:51.480 --> 00:13:56.040
lunch 2 days ago. Our emotions make

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:57.800
everything else feel much more real and

00:13:56.040 --> 00:14:00.920
memorable. So, that when you speak your

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:03.200
new reality, make sure to feel it. Don't

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.960
just say, "I am abundant." Like, close

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:07.040
your eyes and feel what it would feel

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:08.640
like to check your bank account and to

00:14:07.040 --> 00:14:10.880
see more than enough and feel that

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:13.360
relief in your body.

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:14.800
Ah, feel the exhale and the spaciousness

00:14:13.360 --> 00:14:17.080
and just like release, you know, and

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:18.000
then say it from that place. "I am

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.800
abundance." [music]

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.000
Like, you can go on vacation tomorrow

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:24.240
and for the next 3 months. That emotion

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:26.480
makes that declaration feel even more

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:30.240
real to you and so much more powerful.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:32.200
K, keep it sacred. Not every declaration

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:34.240
needs an audience. In fact, some of the

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:36.760
most powerful spoken word you will ever

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:38.920
do is when you do it alone on your own,

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:40.720
in front of the mirror, on your own, on

00:14:38.920 --> 00:14:42.839
a walk, in your car. And there's a

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:45.560
reason why so many spiritual and

00:14:42.839 --> 00:14:48.839
religious traditions emphasize spoken

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:51.480
prayer, mantra, incantation, chanting

00:14:48.839 --> 00:14:53.480
done privately and repeatedly between

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:56.640
you and between God or the universe.

00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:58.280
Repetition in a safe, contained space

00:14:56.640 --> 00:15:01.000
builds neural pathways without the

00:14:58.280 --> 00:15:02.800
interference of other people's doubt or

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:04.640
their judgments. I'm not saying don't

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:06.280
share your goals at all. I'm saying be

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:08.400
intentional about who you share them

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:10.600
with. Maybe don't even share it so

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:13.040
early. Some dreams need to be spoken

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:15.520
into existence privately before you're

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:18.400
strong enough to survive public scrutiny

00:15:15.520 --> 00:15:20.200
and exposure. So, protect the frequency

00:15:18.400 --> 00:15:22.120
of your words like it matters because it

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:23.640
does. Not everyone deserves to hear

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:25.040
about your becoming. So, let me draw a

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:26.760
line here because sometimes people

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:28.360
conflate declarations versus

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:30.440
affirmations and they're actually not

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:32.280
the same thing. An affirmation is a

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:35.080
statement that you want to come true.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:37.160
I'm rich. I'm beautiful. I'm love. And

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:38.880
I'm not against affirmations at all. I

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:40.200
love them and I've talked about them a

00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:41.800
lot on this channel. They are so

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:43.720
powerful to me. But, research from the

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:45.800
University of Waterloo found that for

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:47.640
people with low self-esteem, repeating

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:49.960
positive affirmations actually made them

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:51.680
feel worse. Because if the gap between

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:54.120
what you're saying and what you believe

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:56.280
is too wide, then your brain registers

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:58.480
it as a lie. And trying to lie to

00:15:56.280 --> 00:16:00.760
yourself creates cognitive dissonance,

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:03.600
which creates more stress, not less. A

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:05.800
declaration, however, is different. A

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:08.560
declaration is actually a decision

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:11.040
that's spoken out loud, and decisions

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:14.240
are portals to a new state of mind. The

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:16.160
declaration is the driver that takes you

00:16:14.240 --> 00:16:17.720
there. It's not just I hope this comes

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:19.960
true for me someday, it's I have

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:22.080
decided. That's who I'm becoming. So,

00:16:19.960 --> 00:16:24.280
the energy is very different. A

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:26.400
declaration really announces your

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:28.880
intention. So, think about it like this.

00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:30.440
When the country declares independence,

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:32.880
it doesn't ask another country for

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:34.480
permission. It says, "We are free now,

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:36.000
starting now." And then it acts

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:37.640
accordingly. So, here's how you bridge

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:39.400
this gap. If affirmations feels like a

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.880
lot to you, instead of saying, "I am

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:43.320
rich," which your mind might reject,

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:44.720
try, "I am becoming someone who builds

00:16:43.320 --> 00:16:46.800
wealth." Instead of saying, "I am

00:16:44.720 --> 00:16:48.880
confident," try, "I'm learning to trust

00:16:46.800 --> 00:16:51.200
myself more every day." So, these

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:53.440
bridging declarations honor where you

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:55.160
are while pointing towards where you're

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:57.120
going. Your brain can accept them

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.560
because they're actually true right now.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.480
You did decide that, that you're

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:02.400
becoming, that you are learning. So,

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:04.600
once your brain accepts that statement,

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:06.760
it starts to build these neural pathways

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:08.040
to support that. Now, are you guys ready

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:09.439
to get even deeper? Because this is

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:10.800
going to make everything make sense.

00:17:09.439 --> 00:17:12.680
Your words don't just reflect your

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:14.439
identity, they actually construct it.

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:16.079
So, every time you say, "I'm not a

00:17:14.439 --> 00:17:17.839
morning person," you are building the

00:17:16.079 --> 00:17:19.640
foundation for someone who can't wake up

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:21.319
early. And every time you say, "I am bad

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:23.560
with money," you are reinforcing a

00:17:21.319 --> 00:17:25.880
financial identity that will sabotage

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:27.160
every budget and every savings plan and

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:29.360
every investment opportunity that you

00:17:27.160 --> 00:17:32.120
come across. Because your behavior

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:34.320
always snaps back to match your spoken I

00:17:32.120 --> 00:17:36.000
am identity. This is why people can

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:38.320
learn about all the right strategies and

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:40.560
read a ton of self-help books and still

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:42.360
never change. Because that person that

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:44.840
they are speaking themselves into is

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:46.840
still the same person who created that

00:17:44.840 --> 00:17:48.720
problem in the first place. You're

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:50.440
trying to build a new life with your old

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:51.920
self and you're not willing to let go of

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.920
that old self. Your words are the

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:56.120
building blocks of that identity. So,

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:58.440
one thing I noticed across every sport

00:17:56.120 --> 00:18:00.120
is how the greatest athletes talk about

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:02.320
themselves. None of them are going to

00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:04.320
sit around and lament about how afraid

00:18:02.320 --> 00:18:06.240
they are of losing. They talk about

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:07.800
mastering their craft. They talk about

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:09.560
who they are becoming and how their

00:18:07.800 --> 00:18:11.760
younger self is so proud of them. Now,

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:13.680
Michael Jordan wouldn't say things like,

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:15.040
"I hope I don't miss." He actually said,

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:17.320
"I have failed over and over again my

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:19.720
life and that I succeed." He talked

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:21.760
about his failure as his fuel and not

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:24.440
who he is. The athletes who win

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:26.560
consistently don't eliminate the fear of

00:18:24.440 --> 00:18:28.560
losing, but they focus their language on

00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:30.920
what they can control while getting

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:32.960
better at what they do. This actually

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:34.680
lowers the internal pressure because the

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:37.040
mental spotlight isn't on whether they

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:39.360
win or lose. Their spoken focus is on

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:41.240
their mastery of their craft and not the

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:43.440
outcome. You won't be focusing on your

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:46.600
defeat when your words are constantly

00:18:43.440 --> 00:18:49.040
about improvement, no matter what. So,

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:51.080
ask yourself right now and be so honest

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:52.480
with yourself, what are the I am

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:54.360
statements that you are most often

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:56.400
repeating in your head? Those are your

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:58.200
real declarations. And especially when

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:59.560
you're speaking it out loud or typing it

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:01.440
out loud or whatever, these are the

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:03.000
spells that you're casting on yourself

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:04.320
every single day. And maybe some of you

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:05.640
guys may think that manifestation

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:07.560
doesn't work, but that's because you

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:09.800
don't really understand how it works. We

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:11.520
are all doing it, no matter what we

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.080
believe. So, try this. I want you to

00:19:11.520 --> 00:19:14.840
start speaking your future before

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:17.040
there's even any evidence for it. For

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:18.800
example, you can try saying, "I am a

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:20.200
successful creator." before you even

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:22.040
have a thousand followers. And I want

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.720
you to try and say, "I am building

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:25.600
something that matters." before you even

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:27.960
have anything to show for it. The thing

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:30.840
about creating transformation is the

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:33.320
evidence always comes after the decision

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:36.080
to start changing our identity, never

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:38.240
before. You never get the proof first

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:40.000
and then start believing. You always

00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:41.440
start believing first before the

00:19:40.000 --> 00:19:43.520
evidence can even catch up and

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:45.240
eventually it does. I remember when I

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:47.600
first started this channel, my first

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:49.880
video had 20 views in 1 week and I said

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:51.360
to myself, "I am helping other people

00:19:49.880 --> 00:19:54.200
transform their lives. If I can even

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:55.960
help one person, I have done my job."

